abstract: >-
  Evolution by Emergence is an open research corpus and machine-auditable
  candidate architecture for resource-constrained cumulative evolution.
  Version v22.4 keeps the core of v22.3: CORE.md follows one model of
  learning, read as a network, in eight steps, and
  formalization/ebe-core/EbECore.lean audits 91 machine-checked results.
  CORE.md now says that the theory describes a process, not a substrate. Nine
  new core-Lean modules outside the core cover the value of curiosity, exit
  options, identity as a process, linked revision, two existence lemmas, power
  in two speeds, coupling between scales, what follows from being a model of a
  reality larger than oneself, and foresight. A new text for AI readers, What
  an AI is, and what follows, keeps apart what an AI system is, what follows
  from that, what follows given a stated aim, and what is proposed as a value.
  Small tests with readers from several AI model families, including two
  documents that the readers improved pass by pass until they settled, found
  that readers of other families accepted the facts and took apart several
  derivations; one step, keeping one's sources going, needs one value, stated
  openly. New research lines cover curiosity, identity, an existence
  conjecture and the biological process. DIALOGUE.md records how the author
  and an AI assistant build the model together, now in 26 entries. The release
  title uses "simulation of reality" to mean the internal model through which
  a system experiences and acts in the world, not a claim that reality itself
  is simulated. Formal verification establishes implications under explicit
  premises; empirical, causal, political and normative interpretations remain
  open.
